<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Changping</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">262–260 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Changping, fought from 262 to 260 BCE near present-day Gaoping in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a>, was the decisive clash between the Chinese states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> and Zhao. The Qin general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bai-qi">Bai Qi</a> surrounded the Zhao army under Zhao Kuo, who was killed. Ancient sources claim that some 400,000 surrendered Zhao soldiers were then massacred, probably an exaggeration, but Zhao never recovered its strength.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-changping.jpg" alt="Battle of Changping" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SY · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Changping.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
